+# Academic review mode
+
+This optional mode adds conservative checks and a candidate audit trail. It keeps the model's trained prompt and sampling unchanged. It does not train a journal-specific model, prove semantic equivalence, certify publication readiness, or promise any detector result.
+
+```bash
+hz paper.md --academic results-in-engineering --json --quiet -o paper.review.md > paper.audit.json
+```
+
+The `--academic` choices are `general`, `nature`, `applied-sciences`, `results-in-engineering`, `caadria`, `clinical`, `materials`, `buildings`, `sustainability`, and `automation-in-construction`. They label the review context in the report; the current automatic checks are the same for all profiles. Choose actual venue and section instructions during human editing. No profile text is injected into the completion prompt.
+
+Supply exact technical names, symbols or phrases using a UTF-8 file, one per line:
+
+```bash
+hz paper.md --academic caadria --protect-file terms.txt --json -o paper.review.md > paper.audit.json
+```
+
+The checks compare occurrences of numbers, recognized adjacent units, bracketed numeric/LaTeX/parenthesized year citations, inline math/code, selected English uncertainty/negation/causal/directional words, and user-protected phrases. They also use existing `hz` checks. Academic mode allows copying: accurate terminology or an already clear sentence need not be paraphrased. It retries any flagged candidate up to `--retries`; if no candidate passes, it keeps the original piece.
+
+Exit 4 means at least one original piece was retained because all candidates triggered checks. Output and JSON are still written. Exit 0 means no automatic alarms, **not** that the science is verified. `--json` is required so the audit can be retained. Save redirected stdout even for exit 4. Existing exit codes 1–3 retain their meaning.
+
+The report contains source and candidate passages, hashes, reasons, selected attempt, profile, sampling and a `review_required` marker. These passages may contain unpublished material; keep the report with the manuscript. The audit contains the final completion of each main attempt, not intermediate language-resampling outputs. The upstream backend reports the model filename; record a model-weight checksum separately for reproducible experiments.
+
+Limitations: regex checks miss many units, formulas, citation styles and meaning changes. They are mainly designed for English; they do not validate Chinese claim scope. Counts cannot ensure that a number or citation remains attached to the correct claim. Legitimate synonyms may trigger fallback. Names need explicit protection. Whole-document consistency and method–code alignment require separate review. DOCX formatting limitations of `hz` still apply.
+
+Review quantities in context, endpoints, comparator definitions, negation, uncertainty, citations and table consistency. Follow current venue disclosure requirements. The original model prompt asks to cut hedging, which is why scientific uncertainty needs explicit checking; these alarms cannot fully resolve that mismatch.
+
+Tests use fake completion servers. No real-model quality or detector benchmark was run for this feature.
